<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The UI ships in the user's own language. The German is the OUTPUT, not the interface.

  THE RULE for the German that stays — one rule, and only one: a German word stays in the
  interface only when the user will meet THAT WORD outside the app, in a job advert, in the
  documents an employer asks for, or as the name of an institution, a law or a standard. Every
  word the app is merely naming for itself stands in the user's language. The words that qualify
  are listed once in ui/GermanTerms.kt, each with the one-line explanation shown where it first
  appears, and GermanTermsTest fails the build if a locale carries a German word that is not on
  that list.

  So: Lebenslauf, Anschreiben, Bewerbungsmappe, Anlagenverzeichnis, Zeugnis, Nachweis,
  Referenznummer, Motivationsschreiben, anabin, DIN 5008 and AGG stay. Zeitstrahl, Abgleich,
  Maschinenlesbarkeit, Betreffzeile, Pensum, Ausbildung, Berufserfahrung and the rest are
  translated — they were never vocabulary the user needed, only untranslated chrome.

  HARD RULE: no emoji in any string here. EmojiFreeStringsTest fails the build if one appears.
-->
